                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Loved the fact that it had default controller mappings for mode 1 and 2, like you would use to fly RC planes/drones.\nThe menu system where you have to look behind you is a bit much, maybe my centre point was off but seemed like I had to turn my head 180degrees to see the track, let me turn my body using the stick or keep menu to 180 degrees or 230degrees max.  \nThe dynamics of how the drones handle are way off....if you've ever flown raceing drones before you'll have a hard time adjusting to this.  Bank and yank does not work well at all, I ended up doing best by flying rudder and \"throttle\" (up/down) only, which kinda defeats the point.\nHad serious frame drops in menu view, on a 1070?\nFun for 30min",
